# Line endings are decided here, not by each contributor's core.autocrlf.
#
# Without this file every checkout's autocrlf setting decides what lands, and a
# contributor whose environment writes CRLF commits an entire file back changed --
# PR #87 reported +3598/-3592 on src/cli/program.ts for six real added lines, and a
# branch editing that file normally then conflicts on every line of it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide which files are text; `eol=lf` fixes what goes into a
# commit. A CRLF working tree still works locally -- only the stored form is pinned.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.onnx binary
